# Question Sets (`SavedQuestionSet`)

Per-subject saved collection of question DB IDs. Parallel to `SavedFilter` and `SavedGenerationProfile` — same `is_starred` / `is_shared` machinery, super-admin-only sharing.

## Model
`SavedQuestionSet` in `app/models.py`:
- `user_id` (FK), `name` (200), `subject` (FK to subjects.id, String(10))
- `question_ids` — JSON list of int Question.id values, materialised at save time (not a formula)
- `is_starred`, `is_shared` (bool, indexed), `created_at`, `updated_at`
- Upsert key: `(user_id, subject, name)`

## API (`app/user.py`, prefix `/user`)
| Route | Method | Description |
|---|---|---|
| `/sets` | GET | Manage page (`saved_question_sets.html`); passes accessible subjects |
| `/sets/list?subject=&show_all=0` | GET | JSON list. Own + `is_shared` (filtered by subject access). `show_all=1` for super admin |
| `/sets/save` | POST JSON | `{name, subject, question_ids:[int]}` — upsert by `(user, subject, name)`. Coerces, dedupes, validates IDs belong to subject |
| `/sets/<id>/data` | GET | `{id, name, subject, question_ids, ...}`. Owner / super admin / shared-with-subject-access |
| `/sets/<id>` | DELETE | Owner or super admin |
| `/sets/bulk-delete` | POST JSON | `{ids:[]}` |
| `/sets/<id>/star` | POST JSON | `{is_starred?: bool}` (toggle if omitted) |
| `/sets/<id>/share` | POST JSON | `{is_shared?: bool}` — **super admin only** |
| `/sets/<id>/rename` | POST JSON | `{name}` — owner / super admin; rejects collisions |

## Dashboard "Set" button + Set Operations modal
Inserted in the question-list header between **Manage** and **Generate**, gated on `current_user.can_generate()`.

Opens `#setOpsModal` (in `templates/dashboard.html`):
- **Sources panel (left)** — four chip kinds (see [dashboard-selection-vs-filter.mdc](mdc:.cursor/rules/dashboard-selection-vs-filter.mdc) for the full taxonomy):
  - `Selection` chip — live, mirrors `selectedQuestions`
  - `Filter Result` chip — all DB IDs matching current sidebar filter (across all pages, from `#allQuestionIds`); enables "trim selection to current filter" via `Selection ∩ Filter Result`
  - `Result` chip — last Evaluate output
  - Saved sets — current subject only, grouped Starred / My sets / Shared by admins
- **Expression chip bar**: tap a source chip → it's appended; operator buttons (∪ ∩ \\) and parens append their own chips. Backspace and Clear edit the chip array.
- **Evaluate**: parses the chip array via recursive descent (single precedence, left-associative, parens for grouping) into an AST and evaluates client-side over `Set<string>` of question IDs.
- **Apply actions**: `Replace Selection` (order-preserving), `Append to Selection`, `Save Result as set…`. There is also a "Save current Selection as set…" entry that bypasses the expression. Apply actions are pure category (1) — they never touch the sidebar filter. If `Show Selected Only` is on at the time of Apply, the page re-syncs to the new selection automatically.

### Operators
- **Union (∪)** — `setUnion(a, b)`
- **Intersection (∩)** — `setIntersect(a, b)`
- **Difference (\\)** — `setDifference(a, b)` — left minus right, binary, left-associative
- No `Not` / complement (universe ambiguity).

### ID type
`selectedQuestions` stores **string** IDs (matches checkbox `value`). All chip set IDs are strings. Saved sets are coerced to int on save (server) and back to string on load (client) to match the existing convention.

## Apply via URL
`/dashboard/?question_set_id=<id>` — fetches `/user/sets/<id>/data` and behaves per the selection-vs-filter policy:
- **Same subject** as the persisted dashboard subject → category (1): replace `selectedQuestions` only, do NOT touch sidebar filter, do NOT auto-submit. `Show Selected Only` is auto-enabled so the user immediately sees the set.
- **Different subject** → switch subject (which would normally clear selection — bypassed via `suppressSelectionClearOnSubjectChange`), reset sidebar filter to subject-only defaults (old topic IDs are stale), seed selection from the set, auto-submit, auto-enable Show Selected Only.

Implemented next to the existing `?profile_id=` and `?filter_data_id=` handlers in the dashboard `DOMContentLoaded` hook. See [dashboard-selection-vs-filter.mdc](mdc:.cursor/rules/dashboard-selection-vs-filter.mdc) for the full URL-handler matrix.

## Permissions
| Operation | Owner | Super admin | Other w/ subject access |
|---|---|---|---|
| List | yes | yes | yes (only `is_shared`) |
| Read `/data` | yes | yes | yes if `is_shared` |
| Create / Save | yes (must have subject access) | yes | yes (must have subject access) |
| Delete / Rename / Star | yes | yes | no |
| Toggle Share | no | yes | no |
